{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"e8d5a8de3e30e964","type":"text","text":"# Search","x":-466,"y":-159,"width":126,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"b8d2fdff8fcafdd0","type":"text","text":"Shodan","x":-60,"y":-340,"width":103,"height":60},
		{"id":"a19abc86b319b194","type":"text","text":"Shodan 1 searc engine hai jo specifically IOT ke liye banaya gaya h ","x":260,"y":-350,"width":328,"height":81},
		{"id":"715ab3def61b51b1","type":"file","file":"2. Cyber Security 101/3. Search Skills/screenshots/shodan.png","x":700,"y":-394,"width":400,"height":170},
		{"id":"1d823cfffd05e1fa","type":"text","text":"Shodan also supports its own query filters, which let you narrow results significantly:\n\n|            |                                                                                             |                                     |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| **Filter** | **Description**                                                                             | **Example**                         |\n| `country`  | Restrict results to a specific country code.                                                | `country:IE`                        |\n| `port`     | Filter by a specific port number or a range.                                                | `port:22`                           |\n| `org`      | Scope results in a named organisation or ASN Identifier (Who owns a range of IP addresses). | `AS7224`  <br>(Amazon Web Services) |\n| `hostname` | Match against a specific hostname or domain.                                                | `hostname:fakebank.thm`             |","x":1260,"y":-438,"width":1000,"height":259},
		{"id":"d1eead8b69835871","type":"file","file":"2. Cyber Security 101/3. Search Skills/screenshots/shodan2.png","x":700,"y":-662,"width":399,"height":224},
		{"id":"8cbae70c88e1106b","type":"text","text":"VirusTotal","x":-60,"y":-20,"width":103,"height":60},
		{"id":"1e9971b47cf91455","type":"text","text":"VirusTotal collates results from over 70 antivirus engines and website scanners into a single interface.","x":260,"y":-32,"width":328,"height":85},
		{"id":"245251b93334c079","type":"text","text":"Submit a file, a URL, a domain, or a file hash. VirusTotal will tell you whether any of those engines have flagged it as malicious or not.","x":243,"y":-196,"width":363,"height":97},
		{"id":"10897dc3c04a4a26","type":"file","file":"2. Cyber Security 101/3. Search Skills/screenshots/virusTotal.png","x":225,"y":140,"width":400,"height":161},
		{"id":"30f546b2c78808a4","type":"file","file":"2. Cyber Security 101/3. Search Skills/screenshots/virusTotal2.png","x":740,"y":-138,"width":400,"height":297},
		{"id":"cd33cad31188ed8c","type":"text","text":"**Vulnerabilities DB (CVE)** ","x":-524,"y":457,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"8e9b30520a5f9b20","type":"text","text":"Each confirmed vulnerability is assigned a unique identifier in the format `CVE-YEAR-NUMBER`, such as `CVE-2025-55182`","x":-180,"y":453,"width":470,"height":69},
		{"id":"dffbac1af7d6f9a7","type":"text","text":"You may have heard of vulnerabilities such as `Heartbleed`, `React2Shell`, and `Log4Shell`. These vulnerabilities are given a score **(CVSS)** based on a variety of factors, such as:\n\n- **Impact -** What damage can this vulnerability lead to?\n- **Complexity** - Is the vulnerability easy to exploit or not? \n- **Availability** - How likely is it that someone can exploit this?","x":-195,"y":620,"width":500,"height":201},
		{"id":"2ae7a21b4c400957","type":"text","text":"# ExploitDB","x":620,"y":691,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c49495b6347797b9","type":"file","file":"2. Cyber Security 101/3. Search Skills/screenshots/vulnerabilitydb1.png","x":-399,"y":1160,"width":400,"height":278},
		{"id":"3f92251b7b0dac76","type":"file","file":"2. Cyber Security 101/3. Search Skills/screenshots/vulnerabilitydb2.png","x":140,"y":1160,"width":400,"height":179},
		{"id":"5965d8f5c4ce5561","type":"file","file":"2. Cyber Security 101/3. Search Skills/screenshots/exploitdb.png","x":545,"y":860,"width":400,"height":187},
		{"id":"8204abc34a26d9d2","type":"text","text":"#### Technical Documentation","x":-940,"y":-159,"width":261,"height":60},
		{"id":"e7d67d8e7c03fda9","type":"text","text":"## Linux Man Pages","x":-1362,"y":-291,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"0305dad39084b550","type":"file","file":"2. Cyber Security 101/3. Search Skills/screenshots/linux_man.png","x":-1437,"y":-99,"width":400,"height":302},
		{"id":"bbea98256509319a","type":"text","text":"#### Github","x":-724,"y":-467,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"a9d756f00da2ade7","type":"text","text":"GitHub can be a great resource for staying updated on the latest threats and vulnerabilities. Researchers often publish proof-of-concept (PoC) code, exploitation tools,","x":-823,"y":-640,"width":448,"height":85},
		{"id":"6a5935fa0580626a","type":"file","file":"2. Cyber Security 101/3. Search Skills/screenshots/github.png","x":-1080,"y":-1280,"width":400,"height":301},
